# Settings for .github/workflows/rl-web-judge.yml (sourced by bash; no secrets, ever).
# WebJudge (scaffold/rl/web_judge, docs/specs/web_judge.md) over the judge-layout artifacts of rl-web runs.
# Launch: push to a branch named bench-cloud/rl-web-judge-<anything>.

# Space-separated rl-web workflow run ids, each optionally LABEL=RUN_ID or LABEL=RUN_ID:ARTIFACT_GLOB.
# Each entry is judged as one run; with two or more, every run is compared with the first (exact McNemar).
RUNS=""
# Artifacts to download from each run when an entry has no :ARTIFACT_GLOB.
ARTIFACT_PATTERN="rl-web-*"

# o4mini = the official judge (OpenAI, secret OPENAI_API_KEY) | dry = estimate only, no call.
# webjudge7b needs a GPU server: use kaggle/web-judge instead of this workflow.
BACKEND="o4mini"
# Hard cap in USD for the o4mini backend: the judge stops before any call that could pass it and writes
# partial results. Expect ~$0.10 per task at standard prices (~$30 per 300 tasks) -> see the dry-run step.
MAX_USD="12"
# standard | flex. flex = the same o4-mini at half price, slower, may answer 429 under load (retried).
SERVICE_TIER="standard"
# o4-mini max_completion_tokens per call (reasoning + answer); also the cap's per-call worst case.
MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS="8192"
WORKERS="4"
IMAGE_WORKERS="8"
# Optional URL of a {task_id: level} JSON (or the Online-Mind2Web task list) for by-level rates when the
# harness does not write "level" into result.json. Empty = use result.json only.
LEVELS_URL=""
# Pillow as pinned by upstream requirements.txt (JPEG re-encoding of screenshots).
PILLOW_PIN="Pillow==11.1.0"
